   Environm; China Univ Geosciences; Univ S Australia, CRC CARE; China
   Assoc Sci \& Technol, China Ctr Int Sci \& Technol Exchange; OPCW},
Abstract = {Rice grown in the South-Central USA tends to accumulate a larger
   fraction of methylarsenic species than rice grown in other regions, and
   the reason for these patterns are not clear. The goal of this study was
   to determine how soil management conditions influence the persistence
   and plant uptake of methylarsenic species in rice paddy soils, using
   field-scale experimental plots in Arkansas, USA. We expect methylated
   arsenic to persist in pore water and be more abundant in biomass in
   continuously flooded grown rice.},
