   Versus Exclusion, BROWN UNIV, PROVIDENCE, RI, 1996},
Abstract = {Justice has the illusion of solidity and immutability, but standards for
   fairness change with context. This article presents a conceptual
   analysis that describes the justice arguments used in the affirmative
   action debate as the how, what, and who of affirmative action. The
   article illustrates these procedural, distributive, and exclusionary
   arguments with examples, compares support with opposition, and examines
   conditions that change perceptions of justice over time.},
