Note = {2025 World Environmental and Water Resources Congress, Anchorage, AK,
   MAY 18-21, 2025},
Abstract = {San Francisco is the only coastal city in California, and one of the few
   on the West Coast of the United States of America, that uses a combined
   sewer system managing both wastewater and stormwater in a single
   conveyance system. During heavy rainfall, the system can be overwhelmed,
   leading to untreated discharges from 43 outfall points into San
   Francisco Bay. This research develops a comprehensive numerical model
   using PCSWMM to simulate San Francisco's storm and sewer infrastructure,
   including transport/ storage tunnels and pump stations, assessing the
   impacts of intensified rainfall on drainage performance. Using
   geographic information systems data and climate change projections, this
   study estimates increased flow volumes and the frequency of combined
   sewer overflows. Results pinpoint areas most susceptible to untreated
   discharges, providing critical insights for enhancing urban drainage
   resilience against future climate change impacts.},
