Abstract = {New media patterns generate more complicated and diversified space
   forms. Spatial experiences that are instant, fragmented,
   reality-virtuality interlaced are ubiquitous. Such interlacing brings an
   enormous impact on traditional Chinese streetscapes, increases the risks
   of the fragmentation of streetscapes, and leads to the disorder of
   visual aesthetics. Moreover, it necessarily imposes a great impact on
   traditional street aesthetics, and causes various psychological
   conflicts. This study aims to describe this phenomenon and try to
   explore the reason behind it in new view.},
