   Chartered Inst Bldg (CIOB); Council Sustainable Dev; Emerald; Hong Kong
   Inst Architects; Hong Kong Institut Engineers; Hong Kong Inst Surveyors;
   HKSTS; IUE; JSCE; RICS; Urban Planning Soc China; China Civil Engn Soc},
Abstract = {Transport impacts on natural environment have been addressed in a large
   literature. Increasingly, ecological footprint analysis, an ecological
   accounting tool for measuring human impacts on natural environment, has
   been used to study transport impacts. These studies often estimate
   transport footprint based on traffic volumes collected at traffic survey
   stations. However, the estimates cannot be produced when traffic volume
   information is not available. This study proposes to use the Kriging
   method for estimating transport footprint for road segments where
   traffic volume information is unavailable. Specifically, this study
   estimates transport footprint in 2000 in Houghton County, Michigan by
   using the Ordinary Kriging algorithm and traffic counts collected in
   traffic stations of five neighboring counties. The estimated transport
   footprint is illustrated in graduated colors, buffering, and 3D. The
   results show that the Kriging method is an effective approach for
   estimating transport footprint at local levels where data are limited.},
