   \& Hlth; Int Council Res \& Innovat Bldg \& Construct; European Commiss
   Asia Pro Eco Programme Promot Sustainable Solut Environm Europe \& Asia;
   Korean Soc Indoor Environm; Soc Indoor Environm},
Abstract = {Six residences were selected to evaluate the indoor-outdoor
   characteristics of PM(2.5) carbonaceous species in Hong Kong during
   March and April 2004. Daily (24-h average) indoor/outdoor PM(2.5)
   samples were collected on pre-fired quartz-fiber filters with
   mini-volume samplers and analyzed for organic and elemental carbon (OC,
   EC). The average indoor OC and EC concentrations of 17.1 mu g/m(3) and
   2.8 mu g/m(3). The average indoor OC/EC ratios were 5.8, 9.1, and 5.0 in
   roadside, urban, and rural areas, respectively; while average outdoor
   OC/EC ratios were 4.0, 4.3, and 4.0, respectively. The average I/O
   ratios of 24 h OC, and EC were 1.8, and 1.2, respectively. A simple
   model implied that about two-thirds of carbonaceous particles in indoor
   air are originated from outdoor sources.},
