   CHEMICAL SCIENCE (AEECS 2021)},
Series = {E3S Web of Conferences},
Year = {2021},
Volume = {245},
Note = {5th International Conference on Advances in Energy, Environment and
   Chemical Science (AEECS), ELECTR NETWORK, FEB 26-28, 2021},
Abstract = {To improve the power generation of microbial fuel cell (MFC), the
   cathode is modified to increase its oxygen reduction reaction (ORR)
   activity by using Co/UiO-66, which derived from pyrolyzing the mixture
   of Co(NO3)(2) as the metal precursor incorporated with NH2-UiO-66. It
   was found that Co/UiO-66 (MOF-900) has been developed as a
   high-performance electrocatalyst for ORR at a pyrolysis temperature of
   900 degrees C. Therefore, Co/UiO-66 should be a promising oxygen
   reduction catalyst for application in MFCs. This study provides
   technical and theoretical validation for the MFC performance improvement
   by ORR active MOF-derived catalysts modified cathodes.},
