   MALTA, SEP 09-11, 2009},
Organization = {Wessex Inst Technol; WIT Transact Ecol \& Environm},
Abstract = {Water supply, especially in urban areas, is one of the most important
   issues all over the world. Tritium (3H or T) as a natural radioactive
   isotope of hydrogen with a half-life (T1/2) of 12.26 years has been
   accepted as an efficient tool in groundwater hydrology. By using an
   appropriate model, relevant hydro meteorological and isotope data, a
   computer program which implements an adequate recursive equation, the
   volume of the reservoir under the Galicica Mountain that recharges the
   St. Naum, Spring as well as the Mean Residence Time (MRT) of the ground
   water has been determined and the respective values are V=3.7 x 10(9)
   m(3) and MRT= 6 years.},
