Year = {2015},
Volume = {21},
Number = {6, SI},
Pages = {1948-1951},
Month = {JUN},
Note = {International Conference on Business, Management, Tourism and
   Hospitality (BIZMATOUR), Malacca, MALAYSIA, MAY 12-14, 2015},
Abstract = {ISO 9001 is an international quality standard that emphasized how an
   organization can apply a quality management approach to achieve
   sustained success. Since the automotive industry plays an important role
   in the economy of Malaysia and there has been little study on
   International Organization for Standardization (ISO) certification and
   overall organizational performances for the automotive industry, this
   case study is conducted for a Malaysia automotive company (named as
   Company C) to investigate the awareness in terms of knowledge,
   perceptions and attitudes of their potential customers towards ISO 9001
   certification in the automobile industrial. The relationship between ISO
   certification and overall organizational performances is also
   investigated. In conclusion, the results of the survey on the awareness
   of quality management standards indicate: about 93\% respondents have
   good knowledge of ISO certification; 94.5\% of the respondents show
   perception of quality influences their buying behavior; and 73.5\%
   respondents have positive attitude towards ISO certified motorcycle. The
   potential customers possess greater levels of trust and confidence in
   ISO certified automobile, thus ISO certification creates higher
   potential business opportunities. Besides, the certification could be a
   good marketing tool for an automobile industry. However, ISO
   certification alone does not influence the overall organizational
   performances. A business needs a better quality strategic plan to be
   able to compete internationally.},
