Note = {7th International Symposium on Highway and Urban Pollution, Inst Quimic
   Sarria, Barcelona, SPAIN, MAY, 2002},
Abstract = {The sources and composition of airborne particles, and trends observed
   over the past 50 years are reviewed in this paper. Major components of
   recent samples include elemental and organic carbon, secondary ammonium
   sulphate and ammonium nitrate, resuspended dust, and soil and sodium
   chloride. Early measurements employed the black smoke technique. More
   recently, PM10 has been the accepted measure and is the basis for air
   quality standards and limit values. Between 1970 and 1999, a substantial
   reduction in emissions of particulate matter was achieved mainly through
   a cut in emissions from commercial, residential, and institutional
   combustion. Forthcoming European Union standards are likely to require
   particulate traps on new diesel vehicles. (C) 2004 Elsevier B.V. All
   rights reserved.},
