   from the Perspective of Value Net},
Booktitle = {PROCEEDINGS OF THE 7TH EURO-ASIA CONFERENCE ON ENVIRONMENT AND CSR:
   TOURISM, MICE, HOSPITALITY MANAGEMENT AND EDUCATION SESSION, PT II},
Year = {2012},
Pages = {183-188},
Note = {7th Euro-Asian Conference on Corporate Social Responsibility and
   Environmental Management, Freiberg, GERMANY, AUG 25-27, 2011},
Organization = {German Acad Exchange Serv Fdn; IMRE Alumni Network},
Abstract = {Starting with the relationship between exhibitions and regional
   economics, this article analyzed the forms and methods of business model
   innovation in international exhibitions with the reference of the Value
   Net Theory. The author pointed out that the management on international
   exhibitions is inclined to evolve from Industry Chain Collaboration to
   Integration of Regional Value Net. Four ways of business model
   innovation in exhibitions, including integration, correlation, feedback,
   and cross-linking, were proposed together with their supporting
   conditions. Moreover, the author suggest local governments to adjust
   urban exhibition management from direct operations to indirect
   regulation; to promote new methods for value creation by means of
   industrial and regional coordination policies, and to enhance the
   economic benefits of exhibitions.},
