   SEP 09-13, 2002},
Organization = {Int Assoc Housing Sci},
Abstract = {Century old building stock, monuments, and sculptures have started now
   dwindling and disappearing due to many reasons such as fatigue, climatic
   variations, natural and man made calamities like floods, cyclones,
   earthquakes, fires, accidents and civil \& international wars etc. The
   new buildings are coming up also on mass scale to cope up with the
   present demand. The new technologies, materials, and skills have made
   this possible. However, the climatic changes are so vast and irregular
   and cyclones and earthquakes have disturbed the eco balance in sky and
   below \& above earth making people's life miserable. The economic growth
   in the new millennium has continued the pace of last five decades but it
   is nullified or made truncated by nature. The buildings of all kinds
   residential, commercial, and social are severely affected by ravage of
   cyclones, floods, and earthquakes etc. which have become frequent.
   Hence, rehabilitation of buildings is required continuously making old
   stock usable, livable, and new stock maintained by preventive and
   corrective maintenance technology. Population explosion of last
   millennium and economic unbalance and disruption of many, demand
   challenging skills and knowledge to cope up with continuity of problems
   of dwindling resources of materials and finance and complicated and
   expensive to deal with multiple problems of vast habitats of different
   regions and different climatologies; and facing different calamities.
   Establishment of Important database, its use and prompt and correct
   assistance and help of technologies, finance and management together
   with short term and long term research programmes, their planning,
   extension and use are stressed to cope up with the present challenges.
   International co-operation on wide spectrum as above is stressed to make
   solutions available economically and promptly.},
