   Priority, at the 99th Annual Convention of the
   American-Psychological-Association, SAN FRANCISCO, CA, AUG, 1991},
Organization = {AMER PSYCHOL ASSOC},
Abstract = {Associations of sexual assault history with multiple measures of
   physical health were examined among randomly selected women living in
   Los Angeles (N= 1,610). Sexually assaulted women were more likely than
   nonassaulted women to report poor health perceptions, functional
   limitation, several chronic diseases, medically explained somatic
   symptoms, and medically unexplained somatic symptoms. Sexual assault was
   associated with increased risk of symptoms in a variety of organ systems
   rather than solely reproductive or sexual symptoms.},
