   1999},
Abstract = {The focus of this chapter is on chronic pain in children and potential
   pathways to soothing, based on our theoretical model of the development
   of chronic pain. We examine the psychobiology of pain transmission,
   including neural visceral and spinal mechanisms, as well as central
   mechanisms likely involved in pain perception. Individual differences in
   pain vulnerability within this context are examined, and we offer
   strategies for soothing the child with chronic pain within this
   psychobiologic perspective.},
